{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100}, "sp": "fc", "rep": 206, "hyps": [{"edit_param": "learning_rate_init", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "lower", "why": "Raising an already large learning rate pushes Adam into divergence, causing large accuracy collapses (e.g. -10 to -59 pp)."}, {"edit_param": "learning_rate_init", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "low", "direction": "higher", "why": "At tiny learning rates training is under-converged in 243 epochs, so increasing the rate improves accuracy."}, {"edit_param": "alpha", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "alpha", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "lower", "why": "At already large L2 penalties, further increases cause underfitting and sizable accuracy drops."}, {"edit_param": "alpha", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "alpha", "cond_band": "low", "direction": "higher", "why": "At negligible L2 penalty a step up has essentially no effect, unlike the strong harm seen at high alpha."}, {"edit_param": "batch_size", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "higher", "why": "Larger batches reduce gradient noise and stabilize training at aggressive learning rates, recovering lost accuracy."}, {"edit_param": "batch_size", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "low", "direction": "lower", "why": "With a tiny learning rate, larger batches mean fewer updates and worse convergence within the epoch budget."}, {"edit_param": "depth", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "lower", "why": "Deeper networks are less stable at large learning rates, so adding a layer often causes training to collapse."}, {"edit_param": "depth", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "low", "direction": "higher", "why": "At low learning rates added depth gives extra capacity without instability, helping under-trained models